Perusal of the judgments, as passed by the Hon'ble Supreme Court, demonstrates that scope of interference in the case of acquittal is very limited and the same would be .
warranted by the High Court only if the judgment of acquittal suffers from patent perversity; that the same is based on a misreading/omission to consider material evidence on record;
and that no two reasonable views are possible and only the view of consistent with the guilt of the accused is possible from the evidence available on record.
